==English==

===Etymology===
Ultimately from Latin ''féminīnus'', from ''fémina'' (woman). (See ''[[feminine]]''). ''Feminist'' first recorded in English 1894, from French ''féministe'' (1872). See also ''[[feminism]]''.

===Pronunciation===
*{{IPA|/ˈfɛmənɪst/}}
*{{SAMPA|/"fEm@nIst/}}

===Adjective===
'''feminist'''

#Relating to or in accordance with [[feminism]].

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

#A person who supports the equality of women with men. 
#A member of a feminist political movement.
#One who believes in the social, political, and economoical equality of the sexes.

===Related words===
*[[feminism]]
*[[feminine]]

===Derived terms===
*[[feminazi]] or [[femi-Nazi]] (pejorative)



